d","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-02-06T13:58:59Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T16:34:34Z","closed_at":"2025-02-07T16:25:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.beta2 (v4.4.beta2.official [a013481b0])\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta2 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6603) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12500H (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI am trying to create a background to labels using PanelContainers. The label and the panel should be centered (texture_width/2) all the time. If there is no text, we can hide. Otherwise, both should be horizontally centered. After launching the game, we can change the text with the LineEdit on the top-left:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52360912-2484-4efe-a3b7-dfa68fc7d2dd)\n\nIt works as expected, meaning the background also gets wider, but if a text is then smaller (for example using Backspace), the background (PanelContainer) stays as before. Positioning seems to be working.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Run project\n- Write some text on the top-left and see the change of the size of panel container (longer than Hi)\n- Delete characters.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c8824d85-0314-4a75-ba63-0bd31aee9c59)\n\nThe background should be as small as `A` and it should be centered above the icon.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[testbug_2025-02-06_14-52-54.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18691023/testbug_2025-02-06_14-52-54.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"vgezer","id":231068,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIz